\title{fass: Fast Approximate Stochastic Search for Spike-and-Slab Variable Selection}
\description{
Scalable Bayesian variable selection for linear regression with very large sample sizes and misspecified (M-open) model spaces. Implements Fast Approximate Stochastic Search (FASS), a model search that scores candidate models with a first-order surrogate for the posterior odds under continuous Gaussian, Laplace, or Student-t spike-and-slab priors. After a one-time pre-computation each search iteration costs O(p), independent of the sample size. Student-t spikes and slabs are robust to model superinduction, the tendency of posterior odds to favour ever larger models as n grows when no candidate model is correct. Selected models can be followed by post-hoc posterior inference via block or mean-field variational Bayes, expectation propagation, Laplace approximation, or Gibbs sampling. Standard, partially collapsed, and skinny Gibbs samplers (Narisetty, Shen and He (2019) \doi{10.1080/01621459.2018.1482754}) are included as benchmarks, along with posterior predictive scoring (CRPS).
}
